From: snowf14k3 <60956553+snowf14k3@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 22:57:39 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] media: venus: vote an IRIS1 operating point before boot

Set the lowest configured operating point before enabling IRIS1 core
clocks. Merely finding an OPP without applying it leaves the first
firmware boot dependent on a bootloader clock and voltage vote.
Use dev_pm_opp_set_rate so the required power-domain performance vote
is applied together with the core rate rather than bypassed by a raw
clk_set_rate call.

Reference: Android Q sm8150.dtsi pil Venus node specifies 200 MHz core
and AHB proxy rates; VPU5 __venus_power_on() also scales clocks before
firmware resume. Final rates must match the selected silicon revision.

No new rates or voltage levels are invented here. Platform OPP data
is a prerequisite for using this branch. Validate cold boot and idle
resume for both decode and encode, not just a warm firmware session.

Signed-off-by: snowf14k3 <60956553+snowf14k3@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/pm_helpers.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/pm_helpers.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/pm_helpers.c
index 5d04a57c5..38d4abc47 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/pm_helpers.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/pm_helpers.c
@@ -58,6 +58,12 @@ static int core_clks_enable(struct venus_core *core)
 		dev_pm_opp_put(opp);
 	}
 
+	if (IS_IRIS1(core)) {
+		ret = dev_pm_opp_set_rate(dev, freq);
+		if (ret)
+			return ret;
+	}
+
 	for (i = 0; i < res->clks_num; i++) {
 		if (IS_V6(core) || (IS_V4(core) && is_lite(core))) {
 			ret = clk_set_rate(core->clks[i], freq);
-- 
